# Tracer: trusted object declarations and their exact Result effects
#
# Before: `trust have` was executable by Litex but had no
# StmtResult-to-Lean statement route.
#
# Now: each trusted object is emitted as an explicit Lean axiom at the same
# source trust boundary. Its parameter-membership store keeps the Runtime
# FactId, and attached trusted facts are emitted in their retained store order.
# The later application resolves the function contract and WD-produced return
# membership through those exact FactIds.
#
# Boundary: this tracer covers ordinary object carriers with no inferred
# sibling facts. Trusted set/refined-set declarations and parameter stores
# with inference children remain fail-closed.

trust have f fn(x R) R

trust have a R:
    a = a

f(a) $in R
